Task: German Legal Named Entity Recognition
Description: Recognize named entities in German legal text. Entities to look for: organisation, person. German capitalizes all nouns, so rules must use strong context anchors 

Input schema: {'text': 'str'}
Output schema:
entities: List[Entity]

Entity:
  text: string  # The matched text span
  start: integer  # Start character offset
  end: integer  # End character offset
  type: string  # Entity label

AVAILABLE ENTITY TYPES: ['organisation', 'person']
Rules MUST use one of these types in output_template.

TRAINING EXAMPLES (20 shown):

Input: {"text": "Gericht OGH"}
Output: {"entities": [{"text": "OGH", "type": "organisation", "start": 8, "end": 11}]}

